From: The VIctory, DexNom and PortVI contributors
Subject: Probe center pixel I/J in D3D primitive order with an opt-in feature
Upstream: https://github.com/Marvisak/VIctory/pull/281 (d9bbff571eabf7defe6b106349acda49d1eaa3f8)
Upstream: https://github.com/Marvisak/VIctory/pull/442 (b6ccc95950ab6d694671acf5cb6c72fa957e31ee)
Upstream: https://github.com/DexNom/VIctory/tree/64bd58f5fb794216894bc0e33e03a3a64d19c347

This experimental translation uses API-order triangle weights. A GFX10.3
primitive can rotate the vertex order, so the normal translation and its
cached results remain separate. The test uses a source-built shader and
checks direct perspective and no-perspective center weights by readback.

